language 0.1.0
module messaging
  means
    Exchange of self-contained messages between loosely coupled parties: the
    meaning of messages, channels, subscriptions and facts of delivery.

entity event : thing
  means
    event: an immutable fact about a change that occurred or a state observed.

entity command : thing
  means
    command: an addressed intent to have a definite action performed.

entity message : thing
  means
    message: a self-contained unit of transferred data representing an event,
    a command or another exchange.

entity channel : thing
  means
    channel: a logical path along which messages travel from publishers to
    subscribers.

entity publisher : thing
  means
    publisher: a party placing messages into a channel.

entity subscriber : thing
  means
    subscriber: a party having declared an interest in receiving messages from
    a channel.

entity delivery : thing
  means
    delivery: a single attempt to convey a particular message to a particular
    recipient.

entity subscription : thing
  means
    subscription: a lasting rule binding a subscriber to the messages of a
    channel that concern it.
